@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix obo:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/> .
@prefix ies:  <http://ies.data.gov.uk/ontology/ies4#> .

<https://example.org/ontology-tradecraft/ies-mapping> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:comment "IES -> BFO mappings, the IES-side view of bfo-mapping.ttl." .

### The matched pair is BFO process <-> ies:Event (see bfo-mapping.ttl). The enrichment axioms on that
### pair relate ies:Event to ies:ParticularPeriod, and BFO process to temporal regions. An IES
### ParticularPeriod is a specific stretch of time (a year, a day, an instant encoded in UTC), which is
### what BFO calls a temporal region (BFO_0000008: "an occurrent over which processes can unfold").
ies:ParticularPeriod rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000008 .
